[2.099, "o", "#"]
[0.201, "o", " Target Validation Report: Top 3 Druggable Targets for Type 2 Diabetes\r\n\r\nI have performed a target validation analysis integrating genetic"]
[0.100, "o", " association data, tractability/druggability, global AlphaFold confidence metrics, and representative pathogenic clinical variants for **Type 2 Diabetes Mell"]
[0.100, "o", "itus (MONDO_0005148)**. \r\n\r\nA persistent copy of this document has been saved"]
[0.100, "o", " to [final_report.md](file:///Users/startup/.gemini/antigravity/brain/0def18"]
[0.050, "o", "0ffdb69c63b18c450e67c8429a"]
[0.099, "o", "/final_report.md).\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Ranked Targets Evaluation\r\n\r\n### 1. KCNJ11"]
[0.050, "o", "\r\n*   **Gene Symbol:** KCNJ11\r\n*   **UniProt Accession:**"]
[0.102, "o", " [Q14654](https://www.uniprot.org/uniprotkb/Q14654/entry"]
[0.248, "o", ")\r\n*   **Open Targets Association Score:** **0.865**\r\n*   **Druggability"]
[0.100, "o", " / Tractability:** Highly tractable via Small Molecule (SM). Modality `SM` Approved Drug is **True**, High-Quality Ligand is"]
[0.100, "o", " **True**, and there is a high-resolution structure with ligand bound. \r\n*   **Mean AlphaFold pLD"]
[0.100, "o", "DT:** **83.81** (high prediction confidence for transmembrane pore-forming regions).\r\n*   **Representative Pathogenic Clin"]
[0.051, "o", "Var Variant:**"]
[0.100, "o", " [NM_000525.4(KCNJ11):c.928dup (p.Leu310fs)](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/"]
[0.050, "o", "clinvar/variation/4849669/)\r\n    *   *Clinical Significance:* Likely pathogenic\r\n"]
[0.101, "o", "    *   *Phenotype:* Familial hyperinsulinemic hypoglycemia 2\r\n\r\n### 2. ABCC8\r\n"]
[0.100, "o", "*   **Gene Symbol:** ABCC8\r\n*   **UniProt Accession:**"]
[0.049, "o", " [Q09428](https://www.uniprot.org/uniprotkb/Q09428/"]
[0.100, "o", "entry)\r\n*   **Open Targets Association Score:** **0.865**\r\n*   **Drugg"]
[0.149, "o", "ability / Tractability:** Highly tractable via Small Molecule (SM). Modality `SM` Approved Drug is **True**, High-Quality Ligand is **True**, and there is a high-resolution structure with ligand bound. \r\n*   "]
[0.051, "o", "**Mean AlphaFold pLDDT:** **82.31** (high prediction confidence overall across the 1"]
[0.150, "o", "581-residue multi-span protein).\r\n*   **Representative Pathogenic ClinVar Variant:**"]
[0.101, "o", " [NM_000352.6(ABCC8):c.2051G>A (p.Gly684Asp)](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/clinvar/variation"]
[0.098, "o", "/4818990/)\r\n    *   *Clinical Significance:* Likely pathogenic\r\n    *   *"]
[0.101, "o", "Phenotype:* Familial hyperinsulinemic hypoglycemia 1\r\n\r\n### 3. GCK\r\n*   **Gene Symbol"]
[0.100, "o", ":** GCK\r\n*   **UniProt Accession:** [P35557](https://www.uniprot"]
[0.052, "o", ".org/uniprotkb/P35557/entry)\r\n*   **Open Targets Association"]
[0.098, "o", " Score:** **0.861**\r\n*   **Druggability / Tractability:** Modality `SM` Advanced Clinical"]
[0.150, "o", " is **True**, Structure with Ligand is **True**, High-Quality Ligand is **True**, and High-Quality Pocket is **True"]
[0.199, "o", "**. Multiple GCK activators have progressed to Phase 2/3 trials.\r\n*   **Mean AlphaFold pLDDT:** **93.69** (very high prediction confidence representing a highly stable globular enzyme fold).\r\n*   **Representative Pathogenic ClinVar Variant:**"]
[0.101, "o", " [NM_000162.5(GCK):c.1346C>A (p.Ala449Glu)](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih."]
[0.099, "o", "gov/clinvar/variation/4849222/)\r\n    *   *Clinical Significance:* Likely"]
[0.150, "o", " pathogenic\r\n    *   *Phenotype:* Maturity-onset diabetes of the young type 2 (MODY2)\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Ranking"]
[0.101, "o", " Rationale\r\n\r\n1.  **KCNJ11 (Rank 1):** Exhibits the highest genetic association score ("]
[0.100, "o", "0.865) and forms the pore structure for the ATP-sensitive potassium ($\\text{K}_{\\text{"]
[0.100, "o", "ATP}}$) channel. It is targeted by a widely utilized and highly validated class of approved small molecule therapeutics (e.g. sulf"]
[0.049, "o", "onylureas).\r\n2.  **ABCC8 (Rank 2):** Serves as the key regulatory subunit of the $\\text"]
[0.101, "o", "{K}_{\\text{ATP}}$ channel complexed with KCNJ11. It holds a near-identical association"]
[0.150, "o", " score (0.865) and has well-established, validated small-molecule approved drugs. It is ranked"]
[0.150, "o", " slightly below KCNJ11 due to its high structural complexity as a large multi-domain protein.\r\n3.  "]
[0.050, "o", "**GCK (Rank 3):** Glucokinase serves as the primary pancreatic beta-cell glucose sensor. It"]
[0.201, "o", " presents an exceptional globular structural profile (AlphaFold pLDDT of 93.69) and possesses a structurally validated high-"]
[0.200, "o", "quality binding pocket. Although GCK does not currently have approved drugs on the market, it has multiple small-molecule candidates in advanced clinical stages.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Sources\r\n*   **EuropePMC Search / Literature Validation:** `literature_search`\r\n*   "]
[0.049, "o", "**Open Targets Disease Validation:** `opentargets_search_disease`\r\n*   **Open Targets Target Validation:**"]
[0.151, "o", " `opentargets_associated_targets`\r\n*   **Open Targets Tractability/Druggability Assessment:** "]
[0.263, "o", "`opentargets_target_druggability`\r\n*   **UniProt Sequence & Function retrieval:** `uniprot_search`\r\n*   **AlphaFold Structure Resolution:** `alphafold_fetch_structure`\r\n*   **ClinVar Variant Search:** `clinvar_search`\r\n*   **ClinVar Summary Extraction:** `clinvar_summary`"]
